  faqs={[
    { q: 'What is the SQ3R reading method?', a: 'A five-step active reading method: Survey the section, turn headings into Questions, Read to answer them, Recite the answers from memory, and Review later. It was developed by Francis Robinson to make textbook reading stick.' },
    { q: 'Should I highlight while reading a textbook?', a: 'Highlighting is one of the least effective techniques in the research. If you highlight at all, do it sparingly and only after you understand a section, then convert the key points into questions you test yourself on.' },
